To use templeteref in ag-Grid Angular as cell renderer, follow the steps below:

1. Define the template in your component's HTML file:
```
<ng-template #customRenderer let-value="value">
  <div>{{value}}</div>
</ng-template>
```

2. In your column definition, specify the cell renderer as "agGroupCellRenderer" and include the template reference as "cellRendererParams":
```
<ag-grid-angular
    [rowData]="rowData"
    [columnDefs]="columnDefs">
    <ng-template #customRenderer let-value="value">
        <div>{{value}}</div>
    </ng-template>
</ag-grid-angular>

columnDefs = [
    {
        headerName: 'Custom Column',
        field: 'customField',
        cellRenderer:'agGroupCellRenderer',
        cellRendererParams: {
            innerRenderer: 'customRenderer'
        }
    }
];
```
Here, "customRenderer" is the template reference that we defined in step 1.

3. Now, when the ag-grid renders the cell for the above column, it will invoke the "customRenderer" template and pass the cell's value as "value" to the template.

Note: If your template is defined in a different component, you need to import the component and specify the "frameworkComponents" property in "ag-grid-angular" seeting. And use the component name in "innerRenderer" property instead of the template reference.

